<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch central bank lowers its payout to state.</title>
<headline>Dutch central bank lowers its payout to state.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch central bank will pay out a smaller amount in profits to the Dutch government this year, the bank said in its 1996 annual report.</p>
<p>The report showed that the bank made a profit of 1.79 billion guilders in 1996, of which 1.68 billion will be paid to the government.</p>
<p>In 1995 it made a profit of 2.49 billion guilders of which 2.38 billion was paid to the government.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
